Another class finished.  I've stopped doing random classes now, challenge 
games and the last two un-ascended classes from now on.

Cavemen had shown me the weakness of the class early on in my nethack 
career, so I waited until recently to play them seriously.  This one was the 
third promising one in the last month, one faced the Chromatic Dragon 
unprepared and got flayed alive... the other had his lizard corpse stolen by 
a nymph and then made a statue in
Baalzebub's lair.

This one did better just above minetown I hit the bones of a starved wizard 
who died eating an acidic corpse.  Iktat's Cloak was a no-brainer for a low 
level caveman.  He then found two magic lamps in Minetown... one in the 
lighting store and a second in the hardware store, one was blessed.  The 
altar was cross aligned, and there was no general store.  I made a pile of 
the dwarvish cloaks and bows I had planned on selling for protection money 
in the empty shop and locked up.   I headed back up to do sokoban.  A few 
levels later I had a BoH and headed back to the mines.  Minesend was the 
mimic of the mines ending, I got the luckstone and a touchstone that I later 
blessed.  I was trying to decide what to do with the wish I had canned... I 
settled on the PYEC.  A CoMR is not my idea of an endgame cloak. (Genoless 
makes Oilskin a must.)  I had no way of knowing what scroll ID is, no large 
pile of a single type.  I ended up dropping several one off rings down a 
sink in frustration trying to find a =oSD  My only multiples were levitation 
(good) Poison resistance and cold resistance (useless) and free action and 
TC went down the drain.  I found my slippery cloak just above the rogue 
level IIRC.  The only general store in the game was on DL 22, and I finally 
ID'ed ID.  Three blessed scrolls, no full ID.  I had two ?oGeno (grr)  I 
found the bones of Yumyum the Valk who made wishing for another artifact 
impossible. Mojo, Giantslayer and Frosty went into the bag and would be 
stashed on level 1 for the ascension run.  Down to medusa I used the ring to 
float over.  I made another statue and then smashed both.  The coveted 
silver shield was inside.  I headed back up.  there were no less than four 
temples between DL 19 and 26.  I had a /oEnlightenment and used it to pester 
Ishtar as often as possible, getting a golden glow or two, the passtune and 
finally Vorpy.  EW was one of the other scrolls I knew so I made it +5 at 
that point.  Later, while breaking into vaults with a recharged /oDigging  I 
found Knox on level 25.  With reflection and MR and an AC of ~-20 I decided 
to raid the big vault.  Standing in the zoo I took on the garrison in the 
doorway, advancing to collect my first /oDeath (empty for the moment, thanks 
PYEC) and then patiently waiting for the crowd to step up one at a time to 
die.  Many beheadings later I was untrapping the landmines and collecting 
enough gold to get a naked AC of -2 (I donated the minimum until 0 and then 
150% 6 times after that, getting two more points)  I did not kill any 
preists btw.  Most of the gold went to the one Co-Aligned priest on DL 23. 
I did alot of sacing on that altar.  The temple was 2X3 and that made it 
easy to keep the victims near the altar.

At this point I headed back to the quest portal.  I killed a LOT of 
bugbears.  The stairs in the Chromatic Dragon's lair were on the far side of 
the level and I had a running battle back to the stairs.  Vorpy got the 
lizard about 2/3rds of the way back and I tinned the corpse.  I ended the 
game with a nice collection of tins.

I did the castle, generating the last soldiers and a mess of random barracks 
fodder.  I went in through the back door and got yellow dragon scales.  I've 
done YDSM before and didn't mind doing it again.  The black dragon in the 
corridor might have been a nasy surprise, but the PYEC's telepathy warned 
me, so I waited to open the door then jumped the beast and chowed down. 
Firmly I headed into the corner room to get my reward.  I wished up a 
marker, used the PYEC to recharge and got a second one.  I stashed the wand 
at that point and took my blank paper, markers, and made myself some YDSM. 
I also fully enchanted the rest of my gear as-is.  It was a good mix, I 
didn't fooproof any of my un-damaged gear, none of it got damaged until 
after the sanctum when the cloak got uncursed and burned by a fire trap.

Ghennom was annoying, even with many ?oMM, the wizard and sanctum were easy 
with three wands of death.  The PYEC popped one of them on the way down 
after the 5th recharge.  After the ritual I pulled out my /oW and made 
myself a =oFA.  I will not go near priests without one of these by choice. 
I only had three !oGL, but I cursed them all.  The mysterious force was 
HELL!  I crossed Baal 4 times and Juby's swamp 5 times.  I was really scared 
after gremlins started multipling in the swamp on my third visit.  The last 
visit was the last time i'd be able to cross the swamp in any way without 
wading through them.  After the VotD everything went smoothly, I traded some 
junk for my stashed artifacts and gems on level 1.  I had to drop the 
tinning kit to get unburdened at that point.  The planes were smooth 
sailing, the portal on earth only required three zaps to get to.  Air was 
not bad considering that I didn't have a 1/2 damage aritfact the air 
elementals hit hard, when I didn't teleport them.  The portal on fire was 
not too far and I only had to wander for about 200 turns until the portal 
floated into my bubble on water.  Astral was a bit of a pain, but I had lots 
of /oD charges.  I did death first (left), only losing six max hps.  Famine 
was in the center and I used a few /oD charges and a !oFH along the way. 
Pesty was guarding Ishtar's high temple, the guardian angel had died some 
time ago so I ascended alone.

